<p>Discover the earliest arcade games ever made — now playable thanks to the new DICE emulator!</p>
<p>DICE (Discrete Integrated Circuit Emulator) emulates old arcade machines from the early 1970's at a very high level of accuracy. Since these machines had no CPU, the emulator instead emulates discrete logic components in the circuit board.</p>
<p>This method is very system-intensive, and getting full speed requires at least a mid-range CPU (for single-thread performance) along with the 64-bit version of the emulator.</p>

<h5>The package includes:</h5>
<p class="msg msg--success">21 games (~107 MB)</p>
